{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NpnkbnBfhydfLdEercwqBt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd059-version\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/version: Version Identity Binary\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and code releases\n6\t  (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n7\t  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete,\n8\t  testable artifact that exercises the build pipeline before any utility code\n9\t  exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n10\t  when they need to report their own version.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n14\t  - G2: Provide a version variable that other cmd/ packages can import.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: cmd/version binary\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: |\n22\t            Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n23\t            invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n24\t            by a newline and exits 0.\n25\t      - R1.2:\n26\t          text: |\n27\t            The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n28\t            When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n29\t            \"dev\" as the version string.\n30\t      - R1.3:\n31\t          text: |\n32\t            The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n33\t            git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n34\t            linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n35\t            succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n36\t      - R1.4:\n37\t          text: |\n38\t            When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n39\t            as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n40\t            usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n41\t      - R1.5:\n42\t          text: |\n43\t            The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n44\t            can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n45\t            mechanism.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n49\t  - Build, lint, clean, and install mage targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not specified here.\n50\t\n51\tacceptance_criteria:\n52\t  - id: AC1\n53\t    criterion: \"mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n54\t    traces: [R1.1, R1.3]\n55\t  - id: AC2\n56\t    criterion: \"bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n57\t    traces: [R1.4]\n58\t  - id: AC3\n59\t    criterion: \"bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n60\t    traces: [R1.4]\n61\t  - id: AC4\n62\t    criterion: \"A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n63\t    traces: [R1.2]\n64\t  - id: AC5\n65\t    criterion: \"The version package exports a variable or function importable by other cmd/ packages.\"\n66\t    traces: [R1.5]\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fbb6d3e-426e-46e9-82c6-1b7a22dbf6ee","uuid":"d2728e58-a41c-4173-b2fb-f34b2380d199","timestamp":"2026-05-13T23:59:02.272Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5099/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd059-version.yaml","content":"id: srd059-version\ntitle: \"cmd/version: Version Identity Binary\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N) and code releases\n  (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete,\n  testable artifact that exercises the build pipeline before any utility code\n  exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n  when they need to report their own version.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n  - G2: Provide a version variable that other cmd/ packages can import.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: cmd/version binary\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n            invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n            by a newline and exits 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: |\n            The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n            When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n            \"dev\" as the version string.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: |\n            The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n            git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n            linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n            succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n      - R1.4:\n          text: |\n            When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n            as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n            usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n      - R1.5:\n          text: |\n            The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n            can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n            mechanism.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n  - Build, lint, clean, and install mage targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not specified here.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n    traces: [R1.1, R1.3]\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n    traces: [R1.4]\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n    traces: [R1.4]\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n    traces: [R1.2]\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"The version package exports a variable or function importable by other cmd/ packages.\"\n    traces: [R1.5]\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AGwNfSiTMoHKJ8EW7f6xYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the requirements. Let me implement the cmd/version/main.go file. The task only asks me to implement R1.1 through R1.4 (not R1.5, which is about exporting a variable for other packages - that's not in scope for this task).\n\nLet me review the requirements:\n\n- R1.1: cmd/version package, prints version string to stdout + newline, exits 0\n- R1.2: version set via `-ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\"`, defaults to \"dev\"\n- R1.3: mage build target (not my concern - that's magefiles)\n\n\n- R1.4: --version and -v print same version, any other flag prints usage to stderr and exits 2\n\nSo I need to handle flag parsing where --version and -v both output the version and exit cleanly, while any unrecognized flags should print usage information and exit with code 2. Looking at the SRD requirements more carefully, I see that only R1.5 is actually listed for srd059-version, but the task asks me to implement R1.1 through R1.4. Since R1.3 is about the mage build target in the magefiles directory and that's not in my list of files to modify, I'll focus on implementing the version binary itself with the relevant requirements.\n\nWriting the version command implementation... I'm debating whether to handle extra arguments after the flag or keep the implementation minimal. The spec says any unrecognized flag should trigger an error, but it's silent on trailing arguments after a valid flag like `-v`. I'll stick with checking just the first argument for simplicity—if it's `-v` or `--version`, print the version; otherwise, show usage and exit with code 2.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":156773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fbb6d3e-426e-46e9-82c6-1b7a22dbf6ee","uuid":"9d61c194-d3e7-48d4-b59f-2835ea29a7a6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AGwNfSiTMoHKJ8EW7f6xYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context I need. The SRD specifies a simple binary that prints a version string (set via ldflags, defaulting to \"dev\"), supports `--version`/`-v` flags, and exits 2 with a usage message for unknown flags."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":156773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fbb6d3e-426e-46e9-82c6-1b7a22dbf6ee","uuid":"849c2f04-2045-4e64-be4a-438122e1ddca"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AGwNfSiTMoHKJ8EW7f6xYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RRody2BJHMAEeksMr2otLF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5099/cmd/version/main.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/version prints the repository's last known version tag.\n// Implements srd059-version R1.1, R1.2, R1.4.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\n// R1.2: set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\nvar version = \"dev\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) == 1 {\n\t\tfmt.Println(version)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\tcase \"--version\", \"-v\":\n\t\tfmt.Println(version)\n\tdefault:\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Usage: version [--version | -v]\")\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\n\t}\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":156773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fbb6d3e-426e-46e9-82c6-1b7a22dbf6ee","uuid":"f9ab5f02-1893-43e5-978c-256343f5a83c"}
